  "solution": {
    "explanation": "In a circle at least one of the first and last houses is left alone. So the answer is the better of: the best linear robbery of houses 1..n-1, and the best linear robbery of houses 0..n-2. A single house is a special case because those slices would be empty. Each pass is O(n) time with O(1) space.",
    "code": "class Solution:\n    def rob(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        if len(nums) == 1:\n            return nums[0]\n\n        def line(arr):\n            prev, cur = 0, 0\n            for x in arr:\n                prev, cur = cur, max(cur, prev + x)\n            return cur\n\n        return max(line(nums[1:]), line(nums[:-1]))\n"
  }
